foundation.question_text:
Determine the shortest path between $A$ and $E$ by inspection and state its length.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (B) at (2,2.6);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0.4);
\coordinate (D) at (3.8,0.4);
\coordinate (E) at (4.5,2);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (E) node[midway, above] {$3$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, below left] {$6$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$2$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$4$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (A) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The network shows walking times in minutes between Home ($H$) and School ($S$).
